<title>INDIA: India RBI to receive CRB Capital investor claims.</title>
<headline>India RBI to receive CRB Capital investor claims.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said its department of supervision in Bombay would be available for receiving claims from investors in CRB Capital Markets, a non-banking finance company facing liquidation proceedings.</p>
<p>&quot;The RBI will forward claims so received in Mumbai (Bombay) office to the office of the official liquidator at New Delhi,&quot; it said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Investors may also file their claims directly to the Official Liquidator, Delhi High Court.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
